<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated for a woman of 28 on B-cell therapy for multiple sclerosis. Inactivated influenza and COVID-19 vaccines given today; responses may be reduced while B cells are depleted, but the vaccines still protect and are recommended. Live vaccines are avoided on ocrelizumab; she is immune to measles and varicella. Pneumococcal and recombinant zoster vaccines were completed before and during treatment. The hepatitis B surface antibody check after her two hepatitis B doses has not yet been drawn and will be done with next month&apos;s blood tests. Cervical screening is up to date. Contraception was discussed again: she uses condoms consistently and was offered an IUD or implant for more reliable protection during treatment; she will consider it. [S]<list><item>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines given today.</item><item>Hepatitis B surface antibody with the blood tests before the next ocrelizumab dose.</item><item>Cervical screening next year.</item><item>Stretching and posture work for neck and shoulder strain from practice.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Relapsing-remitting multiple sclerosis on ocrelizumab (G35.A)</content>. No relapse since starting treatment; the re-baseline MRI two months ago showed no new or enhancing lesions. [S]<list><item>Ocrelizumab 600 mg next month, with blood count, immunoglobulins and a pregnancy test beforehand.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>110/70 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 3; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two or three glasses of wine a week; low risk</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; she feels safe</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Cytology two years ago normal; next at three years</td></tr><tr><td>Chlamydia and gonorrhea screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Over 24 and not at increased risk</td></tr><tr><td>HIV, hepatitis B and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>All negative before treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine, about five weeks before the next ocrelizumab dose</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>This season&apos;s mRNA vaccine</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 before treatment, for an adult starting immunosuppressive therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two doses, before and during treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Two doses given; the surface antibody check after the series is due with next month&apos;s blood tests</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Series completed in adolescence</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap three years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Live vaccines (MMR, varicella)</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Immune to measles and varicella; live vaccines are avoided on ocrelizumab</td></tr><tr><td>Contraception counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Condoms used consistently; IUD or implant offered for more reliable protection during treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Dental and vision examination</td><td>Due</td><td>Dental check due; eye examination normal today on fundoscopy, optometry yearly</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, this season (inactivated); COVID-19 mRNA vaccine, this season&apos;s formula [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Farez MF, et al. Practice guideline update summary: Vaccine-preventable infections and immunization in multiple sclerosis. Neurology 2019;93(13):584-594 (PMID 31462584) (2019); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Cervical Cancer: Screening (2018); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Ocrelizumab 600 mg next month with blood tests and hepatitis B surface antibody beforehand. Cervical screening next year. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-12: six months: first 600 mg dose of ocrelizumab, no evidence of disease activity, immunoglobulins, vaccination response, pregnancy planning and her return to performing. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
